{
  "_why": "Role track for the ASSEMBLY LINE, authored under docs/profiling/role-pack-authoring-guide.md as Batch 2 part two's second pack. fam_assembly stays the generic ISCO-unit-8219 interview and fam_assemblers_other the generic minor-821 one; neither is touched. This pack belongs to fam_assembly_line, which binds three NCO occupations directly (job_domain specificity 50 beats unit 40 and minor 30), so a line worker who says 'assembly line' or 'असेंबली' gets line depth and every other assembler keeps the generic pack.",
  "_scope": "WORK ON A PACED LINE -- sub-assembly, final assembly and end-of-line testing, to a takt, with nut runners, torque tools and poka-yoke fixtures. The level ladder (Helper / Operator / Skilled) is asked as assembly_level so the sheet can say which rung the man stands on. Bench and machinery assembly (workshop machines, engines, turbines, printing and textile machinery) stays on fam_assemblers_other, electronics and PCB assembly on the same, and 'assembly fitter' stays with the fitter; none is bound here.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS assembly_experience, asked FIRST, and it is ASSEMBLY_LINE_WORKER.tenureQuestionKey. It cannot be experience_years from qp_universal: phase order runs occupation_specific BEFORE universal_tail, so the universal answer does not exist yet when these items are selected -- gating on it is permanently false. Its options carry value_number ONLY. pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, so a value_text beside the number would turn every gte gate below into a string comparison that is false forever.",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 48 and qp_universal@4 spends at most 18. Tier 0 is 7 items, tier 1 (assembly_experience >= 2) adds 3, tier 2 (>= 5) adds 3 -- a senior walks 13, two fewer than the welder's 15, and 13 + 18 = 31 against the 48 ceiling. The three fresher items are gated assembly_experience <= 0, so a senior never sees them and a fresher, who fails both gte gates by construction, tops out at 7 + 3 = 10.",
  "_sheet": "SECTION B IS READ OFF THE RATIFIED ASSEMBLY LINE REFERENCE RESUME (Deepak Jadhav, page 6), not invented. Its seven rows are Assembly stage, Products assembled, Tools used, Shop-floor practice, Line rate worked to, Drawings and Sector worked, and every one has a question here that fills it. Tools used and Shop-floor practice each carry SIX options plus the escape chip because the page prints six values in each; trimming to the chip guideline would drop a value the ratified sheet shows. Line rate is a BANDED single_select, the welder's plate ruling: the page's cell 'Worked to 90-second takt on final line' is hand-set prose around one figure, a free number would not render through a closed dictionary, and the stage ('on final line') is already assembly_stage's row -- so the sheet prints the band that holds 90 seconds, a RECORDED DIVERGENCE. This pack has no case in role-sheet-parity.render.test.ts yet.",
  "_keys": "NO DIGITS IN ANY question_key OR option_key. Both regexes are ^[a-z_]+$, and slugKey REFUSES a key with a digit at runtime even where the corpus validator historically let it through -- one such key makes the whole pack unparseable, which is why the page's '5S' is option_key five_s. drawing_reading and sector_worked are the SHARED keys other packs already use, deliberately: resume-degradation.ts sheds rows BY KEY (sector_worked first) to keep a sheet on one page, and a private key would opt this trade out of that. The page has no materials or measuring-instruments row, so material_worked and measuring_tools are not asked. assembly_line_product is NOT qp_assembly's assembly_product: that key is an rfs skills question with a different vocabulary, and one key meaning two things across packs is how an answer lands in the wrong row.",
  "pack_id": "qp_assembly_line",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_assembly_line",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "Drafted for owner review. Shop-floor vocabulary NOT yet corrected by a practising assembly line worker -- see docs/registers/trade-content-ratification.md.",
  "_fresher": "Guideline section 11 #1: a fresher's Zone 4 is training, trade test, machines used in the ITI workshop and project work, and the History heading never renders empty. These three items are the ask half; resume-fresher-rows.ts, fed by this role's descriptor, is the render half. The KEYS are read literally by that file and must not be renamed; only the workshop VOCABULARY is trade-specific. The three prompts are the welder's verbatim, so they reuse its served text and its voice clips.",
